			<div class="content" id="post-content-4428724">
									

<p>It's not core to the object, but since it's the debut, I'm gonna say I'm not big on the Supplementary Classification Index. I'm only <em>just</em> warming up to the disruption/danger level stuff that's catching on. I feel like it's downright boring for the Foundation to understand anything mysterious or paranormal in <em>this much depth</em> (the &quot;we're not actually sure why this happens&quot; bit is present in just about every SCP whether it's stated or not), and actual &quot;sciencey technical stuff&quot; should only be included if it aids realism or atmosphere, because real science documents are boring.</p>
<p>Especially 𝒩ness. Isn't 𝒩ness literally &quot;the subjective value of something in the opinion of one now-dead civilian with a serious inferiority complex&quot;? (I guess Damien Pisk liked shark movies less than scientists, but more than criminals.) I see why the Foundation might measure it <em>just 'cuz</em>, but it's not the kind of thing that would appear in a need-to-know header.</p>

							</div>

								
