														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4429292">
									

<p>The 𝒩ness article calls it an objective measure, but my thinking is that even if it's just Fisk's opinion, it kind of <em>is</em> objective with respect to Fisk. Like, &quot;I like Star Wars&quot; is a subjective opinion, but &quot;My opinion is that Star Wars is good&quot; is an objectively true statement. Ergo, any given thing is <em>objectively</em> good or bad in Fisk's opinion.</p>
<p>It's a valid interpretation, though!</p>

