			<div class="content" id="post-content-4429545">
									

<p>Quite honestly, it's not a valid interpretation. There are plenty of concepts and articles on the site that leave lots of room to interpretation and headcanon, but 4517 isn't one of them. There is one interpretation of what 𝒩ness represents, and that is that it is the objective measure of the subjective value<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-124106-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-124106-1')">1</a></sup> of a given object relative to the value Damien Pisk placed on himself, at 0. So why would that value be present within the context of SCI? It's completely useless for them to measure except for the purposes of studying that one specific phenomenon. Additionally, the interpretation you're showing here directly contradicts the original author's intention.</p>
