			<div class="content" id="post-content-4431265">
									

<p>I mean, you argue that there's no reason for the SCI to mention 𝒩ness, and I agree, but that doesn't mean the interpretation is unacceptable. I think it's kinda boneheaded to think 𝒩ness has nothing to do with Fisk, but the article doesn't <em>explicitly</em> state the opposite. Maybe there's an objective unit of something's worth, and Fisk was literally objectively worthless? It's a stretch but it's a conclusion you <em>can</em> come to.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Additionally, the interpretation you're showing here directly contradicts the original author's intention.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><em>La mort de l'auteur</em>. Intention doesn't matter all that much.</p>

